    "summaries": [
      {
        "action_date": "2025-04-02",
        "action_desc": "Introduced in House",
        "text": "<p><strong>Aviation Medication Transparency Act of 2025</strong></p><p>This bill directs the Federal Aviation Administration (FAA) to compile, publish, and annually update a list of medications that may be safely prescribed to pilots and air traffic controllers for the purposes of issuing a medical certification. The list must be publicly available on the FAA website and distributed to those seeking a license and medical&nbsp;certification. </p><p>Currently, the FAA does not have a list of approved medications. However, the FAA does have lists for Aviation Medical Examiners of <em>Do Not Issue</em> medications and <em>Do Not Fly</em> medications.<em></em></p>",
        "update_date": "2026-05-05T21:43:39Z"
      }
    ]
  },
